N2  - HFpEF is a clinical syndrome which can be further refined by invasive hemodynamics, with or without provocation testing. There is increasing recognition of pre-clinical HFpEF and the importance of addressing risk factors and comorbid conditions such as kidney disease and obesity. Novel mineralocorticoid receptor antagonists and glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonists show promise in cardiometabolic syndrome. Remote monitoring devices (pulmonary artery pressure monitoring devices, cardiac rhythm device sensors) improved HFpEF care indeed, while emerging device-based therapies such as atrial shunts warrant cautious optimism. A developing frontier in HFpEF management is targeted treatment of pulmonary hypertension through pulmonary artery denervation and/or pharmacologic therapy.
